<title>USA: N.C. Harris 1 nuke unit seen at full output today.</title>
<headline>N.C. Harris 1 nuke unit seen at full output today.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 880 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Shearon Harris nuclear generating facility was expected to resume full power production later today, the operator Carolina Power &amp; Light Co (CP&amp;L) said Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;We're at 93 percent right, and should be at 100 percent by lunch time,&quot; a CP&amp;L spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The unit, in New Hill, N.C., was shut Thursday to repair a steam leak in a turbine building.</p>
<p>CP&amp;L holds 83.8 percent interest in Harris 1 and North Carolina Eastern Municipal Power owns the remaining stake.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1622))</p>
